  "description": "<p>Discussed on April 5th committer call. This would not change any functionality, but would serve to notify people who might be inclined to develop against the classic AuthN classes that they're going away soon and they may want to spend their time on more forward-looking stuff.</p>\n\n<p>At a later point, we could decide to more forcefully deprecate these by sticking them in a .deprecated sub-package...so they're still usable if people are in a real bind. This was a suggestion by Scott Prater on the mailing list recently.</p>",
